# Lambda shared helpers

- Put **pure** shared helpers in `src/server/api/game/helpers/` (e.g. `seats.ts`, `betting.ts`, `cards.ts`). No DB I/O in helpers.
- Seat queries / mutations live in `src/server/api/table/seating.ts` (not helpers).
- Lambda consumes helpers via one directory symlink: `lambda/consumer/link/helpers` → `src/server/api/game/helpers`.
- **Do not** add new per-file symlinks under `lambda/consumer/link/` for helper modules.
- Entry-point links that remain: `dealing.ts` → `game/dealing.ts`, `hand-lifecycle.ts` → `game/hand-lifecycle.ts`, `table-transaction.ts` → `lib/table-transaction.ts`, `schema.ts` (imported directly by `consumer.ts`).
- New helper files are picked up automatically; ensure `lambda/consumer/tsconfig.json` includes `link/helpers/**/*.ts`.
